[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497047317","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99656#issuecomment-2497047317","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99656","id":2497047317,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U1esV","user":{"login":"RandomShaper","id":11797174,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3MTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11797174?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper","html_url":"https://github.com/RandomShaper","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RandomShaper/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T07:17:05Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T07:17:05Z","body":"Makes sense.\r\n\r\nI'd just want to suggest ways to trying not to clutter the internal, neither the exposed APIs before we know the precise delays are needed by projects. Options (not necessarily exclusive):\r\na) Not exposing the precise ones.\r\nb) Not having an msec version of the precise one, at all.\r\nc) Refactoring the precise one so it's only related to frame pacing. Is there any other known usage for it yet?\r\nd) To avoid confusion, maybe the precise one could be renamed to something else. The docs can already explain the difference, but I can foresee many would just prefer the precise version just because it looks like the best choice.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2497047317/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498011376","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99656#issuecomment-2498011376","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99656","id":2498011376,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U5KDw","user":{"login":"Faless","id":1687918,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2ODc5MTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1687918?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless","html_url":"https://github.com/Faless","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Faless/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T13:22:05Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T13:22:05Z","body":"> a) Not exposing the precise ones.\r\n\r\nIf I understand correctly, this is a Windows only issue.\r\n\r\nThe PR that introduced #99593 also wasn't fixing any issue (i.e. had no issue associated with it).\r\n\r\nSo, if there's a problem on frame pacing on windows like the PR that introduced #99593 claims, that should be handled at the platform level (and have a dedicated issue attached, instead of linking to a blog post).\r\n\r\nWe definitely should not bloat and over-complicate the public API because of some weird windows quirk (which should instead just be documented).","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498011376/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2498037895","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99656#issuecomment-2498037895","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99656","id":2498037895,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U5QiH","user":{"login":"mrsaturnsan","id":32889818,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyODg5ODE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32889818?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan","html_url":"https://github.com/mrsaturnsan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrsaturnsan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T13:33:48Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T13:56:17Z","body":"delay_usec is also not precise on Unix. I tested it on macOS, and it was consistently off by 4-5ms.\r\nWith this PR, the accuracy of precise_delay_usec on Unix is also spot on.\r\n\r\n\r\nAnother benefit o